1
00:00:00,860 --> 00:00:02,660
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:04,577
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:07,197
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:10,456
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,975
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,420
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:16,620
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:19,060
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:24,217
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:26,397
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:29,600
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:35,240
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:40,480
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:42,680
One Piece.

15
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:52,557
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:58,497
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

17
00:00:58,580 --> 00:01:03,877
That legendary place that
the end of the map reveals.

18
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:10,157
Is only legendary till
someone proves it real.

19
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:14,437
Through it all, through
all the troubled times.

20
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:16,817
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

21
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:21,077
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

22
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:24,340
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

23
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:28,237
So come aboard and bring along.

24
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:30,640
All your hopes and dreams.

25
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:33,857
Together we will find everything.

26
00:01:33,940 --> 00:01:35,960
That we're looking for.

27
00:01:37,220 --> 00:01:39,677
There's always room for you.

28
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:42,420
If you wanna be my friend.

29
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:46,780
We are, we are on a cruise.

30
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:49,700
We are.

31
00:02:04,220 --> 00:02:06,720
Oh, my goodness.

32
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:08,270
That

33
00:02:08,353 --> 00:02:15,160
crazy

34
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:16,150
rubber

35
00:02:16,233 --> 00:02:17,180
guy beat Captain Kuro.

36
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:19,877
Not even the Marines
were a match for Kuro.

37
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:23,417
You're a man of a thousand plans,
and this guy still beat him!

38
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:24,330
Just...

39
00:02:24,413 --> 00:02:25,243
just who are you?

40
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:26,840
I'm Monkey D. Luffy.

41
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:30,786
The only time a pirate should
abandon his name is when he dies.

42
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:34,499
I would never lose to a
coward who ditches his name,

43
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:37,297
betrays his friends, and
runs from life on the sea.

44
00:02:37,380 --> 00:02:38,320
Uh, Luffy?

45
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:40,504
I never heard that name before.

46
00:02:40,980 --> 00:02:44,137
You should remember my name
for the rest of your lives.

47
00:02:44,220 --> 00:02:47,632
Cause one of these days, I'm
gonna be king of the pirates!

48
00:02:48,940 --> 00:02:50,220
You are?

49
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,420
Now get out of here!

50
00:02:57,100 --> 00:02:58,900
And never come back!

51
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:11,380
You did good, Luffy.

52
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:19,264
I'd expect even you to collapse
after what you just went through?

53
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:20,530
Say

54
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:24,020
Tell me, why were you so mad earlier?

55
00:03:24,340 --> 00:03:26,157
Because I truly hate people like them.

56
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:28,100
They're so wrong.

57
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:31,317
That is not how friends should act.?

58
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:33,260
What are you talking about?

59
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:35,537
Of course it isn't.

60
00:03:35,620 --> 00:03:40,157
Most pirates aren't the brave, honorable
people you always make them out to be!

61
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:41,500
I want some meat.

62
00:03:41,980 --> 00:03:43,760
Oh, you're unbelievable!

63
00:03:51,540 --> 00:03:55,397
Hey guys, think you can keep everything
that just happened here secret?

64
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:56,680
What? A secret?

65
00:03:56,900 --> 00:03:59,157
Why wouldn't we want to
keep all this a secret?

66
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:00,337
Yeah, why, huh?

67
00:04:00,420 --> 00:04:02,977
We put our lives on the
line to save the village!

68
00:04:03,060 --> 00:04:05,117
Now everyone will change
their opinion of you,

69
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:08,788
so instead of being Usopp the
liar, you'll be Usopp the hero!

70
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:11,340
Really, Usopp?

71
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:14,049
You need to clear up
this misunderstanding.

72
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:16,110
Misunderstanding?

73
00:04:16,193 --> 00:04:18,917
I was known as the Village Liar
because I lied all the time, Ms.

74
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:19,830
Kaya.

75
00:04:20,220 --> 00:04:22,220
They were right not to believe me.

76
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:26,097
Besides, there's no point in scaring
people with something that's already over.

77
00:04:26,180 --> 00:04:30,337
And I seriously doubt that any more pirates
like Kuro and his gang will show up.

78
00:04:30,420 --> 00:04:34,773
There's no reason for pirates to attack
our out-of-the-way little village.

79
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:38,280
So listen up, pretend
this never happened, okay?

80
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:41,960
This was all just another
one of my great big lies

81
00:04:46,280 --> 00:04:48,197
Now I won't force you to, but...

82
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:49,237
No, I can do it.

83
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:52,097
I'll do whatever it takes for
the good of the village, Captain!

84
00:04:52,180 --> 00:04:53,780
Yeah, me too! Me too!

85
00:04:54,020 --> 00:04:55,837
My lips are totally sealed, I promise!

86
00:04:55,920 --> 00:05:00,400
I don't care who you allow is
Call, will you? Will you tell?

87
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:04,730
No.

88
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:11,277
Something just isn't right this morning.

89
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:12,400
Where is Usopp?

90
00:05:13,140 --> 00:05:15,817
It kind of throws everything
off if he's not around.

91
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:17,120
I feel so bored.

92
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:19,030
Mama?

93
00:05:19,860 --> 00:05:23,120
Is that screaming liar guy
not coming to town today?

94
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:25,020
That lying little twerp.

95
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:27,280
Where the heck is he?

96
00:05:28,220 --> 00:05:31,396
You don't think I hurt his
feelings yesterday, do you?

97
00:05:31,740 --> 00:05:32,977
Oh, don't worry.

98
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:35,472
He'll be up to his old tricks in no time.

99
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:36,620
I hope so.

100
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:42,800
Thanks, guys.

101
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:46,237
I wouldn't have been able to
protect the village without you.

102
00:05:46,320 --> 00:05:48,077
Give credit where credit's due.

103
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:52,277
If you'd just stood by and done nothing,
I wouldn't have done anything either.

104
00:05:52,360 --> 00:05:53,320
Yeah, same here.

105
00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:55,437
Who cares about any of that?

106
00:05:55,520 --> 00:06:00,167
I've got my hands on this sweet, sweet
treasure now, and I couldn't be happier.

107
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:05,637
Everything that happened
here today helped me.

108
00:06:05,720 --> 00:06:08,308
I've just come to a
very difficult decision.

109
00:06:08,620 --> 00:06:09,450
Huh?

110
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:18,537
Captain Usopp, what did you
want to talk to us about?

111
00:06:18,620 --> 00:06:22,738
The three of you fought well against
those terrible black cat pirates.

112
00:06:24,100 --> 00:06:27,806
As captain, I'm proud of you for
being so brave and courageous.

113
00:06:28,500 --> 00:06:29,400
Thanks to you,

114
00:06:29,580 --> 00:06:33,137
we overcame our biggest and most important
battle since we formed the Usopp Pirates

115
00:06:33,220 --> 00:06:36,857
five years ago That was when you three
brave soldiers were only four years old,

116
00:06:36,940 --> 00:06:37,770
remember?

117
00:06:37,853 --> 00:06:38,683
Yeah.

118
00:06:38,766 --> 00:06:39,717
Now I know this is sudden,

119
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:43,560
but I've decided that I'm going
to set out to sea by myself!

120
00:06:46,260 --> 00:06:49,966
I'm finally going to leave this
place and become a real pirate.

121
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:56,337
At first I wasn't sure what I would do.

122
00:06:56,420 --> 00:06:59,357
I couldn't decide if I wanted
to stay here forever or not.

123
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:03,257
But once I saw them, I knew
deep in my heart what I must do.

124
00:07:03,340 --> 00:07:07,537
I feel that, as a man, I must
set out to the vast ocean.

125
00:07:07,620 --> 00:07:10,060
So, I'm leaving this place behind.

126
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:14,357
I leave for one reason.

127
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:18,160
When the great pirate flag
beckons, you must heed its call!

128
00:07:21,580 --> 00:07:23,840
Captain, say it isn't so?

129
00:07:25,940 --> 00:07:27,477
You're lying again, right?

130
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:29,277
Isn't that a bit hasty?

131
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:30,717
There's no reason to leave.

132
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:32,237
I thought you loved this village.

133
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:35,837
And what's gonna happen to
the Usopp pirates without you?

134
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:39,197
You've been so good to me.

135
00:07:39,280 --> 00:07:42,297
Guys, I plan to leave without
telling the villagers.

136
00:07:42,380 --> 00:07:44,397
Give them my regards.

137
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:48,677
Captain, no, I don't want to.

138
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:49,757
Don't go, Captain!

139
00:07:49,840 --> 00:07:51,193
Just stay here, please!

140
00:07:53,080 --> 00:07:55,551
Usopp Pirates, do you remember this place?

141
00:07:56,080 --> 00:08:00,080
This is where we first met
and formed the Usopp Pirates.

142
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:08,950
Finished!

143
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:11,580
Hey, it's that liar guy. Huh?

144
00:08:11,760 --> 00:08:12,760
Who are you guys?

145
00:08:12,900 --> 00:08:14,657
And why are you so buddy-buddy with me?

146
00:08:14,740 --> 00:08:15,857
Well, Dai, you're famous!

147
00:08:15,940 --> 00:08:18,440
Yeah, you're a really famous guy.

148
00:08:19,020 --> 00:08:20,240
Right, I know.

149
00:08:20,460 --> 00:08:25,097
You've come face to face with a man that
is known the world over as Captain Usopp.

150
00:08:25,180 --> 00:08:28,474
Actually, everyone in the
village calls you liar, Usopp.

151
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:34,273
Okay, from this day forth, you're
officially members of the Usopp Pirates.

152
00:08:34,940 --> 00:08:36,880
Come on! Man up!

153
00:08:38,660 --> 00:08:40,680
A lot's happened since then, huh?

154
00:08:41,820 --> 00:08:42,857
A Cerberus!

155
00:08:42,940 --> 00:08:44,400
Scare it away!

156
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:46,880
A dragon!

157
00:08:47,680 --> 00:08:48,510
A dragon!

158
00:08:49,920 --> 00:08:51,000
Flower storm!

159
00:08:51,980 --> 00:08:53,640
You're amazing, Captain!

160
00:08:55,100 --> 00:08:58,200
But of course, I'm a
brave warrior of the sea!

161
00:08:59,420 --> 00:09:01,357
Please don't talk about the old days!

162
00:09:01,440 --> 00:09:02,657
I can't stand it!

163
00:09:02,740 --> 00:09:04,975
Pepper's right, it's much too painful.

164
00:09:05,060 --> 00:09:06,797
This kind of life isn't like you, Captain!

165
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:07,717
It's not fun!

166
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:09,957
Why would you say that
you're going to leave us?

167
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:12,800
You're not serious, are you?

168
00:09:13,300 --> 00:09:15,840
You're being stupid, Captain. Stupid.

169
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:26,020
All right, men.

170
00:09:26,180 --> 00:09:27,617
Tell me what all your ambitions are.

171
00:09:27,700 --> 00:09:30,280
When I crawl out, my
dream is to run a pub.

172
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:33,277
My whole life I've wanted
to be a master carpenter.

173
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:35,125
My goal is to become a writer.

174
00:09:35,860 --> 00:09:39,801
Then, swear to me now that each of
you will continue on your paths.

175
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:44,216
Promise me that you will never let
the fires of your ambitions die out!

176
00:09:46,340 --> 00:09:52,040
As of today, our group,
the Usopp Pirates...

177
00:09:59,100 --> 00:10:00,500
...are disbanded!

178
00:10:07,380 --> 00:10:10,197
Now that we've eaten, we
should probably get going.

179
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:11,398
Yeah, you're right.

180
00:10:12,760 --> 00:10:13,780
Here you are.

181
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:15,860
Hello there, miss.

182
00:10:16,020 --> 00:10:17,757
Are you all right being out of bed?

183
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:18,670
Yes.

184
00:10:19,420 --> 00:10:22,560
I think now I can truly
start recovering. You see,

185
00:10:22,680 --> 00:10:26,597
my sickness this last year was caused by
the mental shock of losing both my parents.

186
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:29,856
And Usopp's friendship helped
me start getting better.

187
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:32,800
I can't stay in bed forever, you know.

188
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:37,577
I've prepared a present for
you from the bottom of my heart

189
00:10:37,660 --> 00:10:40,497
to show you how grateful I am
for everything you've done here.

190
00:10:40,580 --> 00:10:42,940
I'd be honored if you'd accept it.

191
00:10:48,700 --> 00:10:49,530
All packed.

192
00:10:50,180 --> 00:10:52,474
Guess it's farewell to this house, too.

193
00:10:59,160 --> 00:10:59,990
Hey!

194
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:08,060
I can't get out!

195
00:11:10,180 --> 00:11:12,340
This stupid backpack!

196
00:11:31,020 --> 00:11:32,620
The real Caravelle!

197
00:11:33,820 --> 00:11:36,720
Are you actually giving this to us?

198
00:11:36,940 --> 00:11:39,120
As a token of my appreciation.

199
00:11:40,680 --> 00:11:42,520
It's a slightly older model,

200
00:11:42,620 --> 00:11:45,914
but I personally designed it
and she sails like a dream.

201
00:11:46,020 --> 00:11:50,880
She has a carvel-made Caravelle with
Latine sails and a central stern rudder.

202
00:11:51,060 --> 00:11:54,640
She's a fine ship and her
name is the Going Mary.

203
00:11:56,740 --> 00:11:58,497
Allow me to explain the rigging.

204
00:11:58,580 --> 00:12:01,168
First, about the Kruger
net yard adjustment.

205
00:12:01,260 --> 00:12:02,257
It may seem a little temperamental.

206
00:12:02,340 --> 00:12:05,917
Hold on, you'd be better off just
explaining the technical stuff to me.

207
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:07,520
What a cool ship.

208
00:12:07,820 --> 00:12:09,157
Have you guys seen the front?

209
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:10,980
It's totally awesome.

210
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:15,897
We've loaded it with all the provisions
you might need on a long voyage.

211
00:12:15,980 --> 00:12:16,810
Thanks.

212
00:12:16,893 --> 00:12:18,445
It leaves nothing to be tired.

213
00:12:18,680 --> 00:12:21,092
That leaves nothing to be desired, idiot.

214
00:12:24,280 --> 00:12:25,751
Somebody stop this thing!

215
00:12:25,940 --> 00:12:27,040
Oh, no, it's time!

216
00:12:28,580 --> 00:12:29,737
Hey, what's he doing?

217
00:12:29,820 --> 00:12:30,650
Looks fun.

218
00:12:30,860 --> 00:12:32,331
Well, we better stop him.

219
00:12:32,420 --> 00:12:35,420
That weirdo is on a collision
course with our boat.

220
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:41,480
Oh, hey, thanks, Kaya. Anytime.

221
00:12:42,480 --> 00:12:43,900
You're really doing it.

222
00:12:44,160 --> 00:12:45,897
You're gonna take to the ocean.

223
00:12:45,980 --> 00:12:46,810
Yeah.

224
00:12:46,893 --> 00:12:50,566
I've decided to get going before
I have time to change my mind.

225
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:53,320
Don't stop me.

226
00:12:53,700 --> 00:12:54,540
I won't.

227
00:12:54,720 --> 00:12:56,544
I know it's time for you to go.

228
00:12:56,840 --> 00:12:58,600
Kaya, don't be sad about it.

229
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:01,657
Just think, the next
time I come back here,

230
00:13:01,740 --> 00:13:06,269
I'll tell you about adventures that'll
sound more like lies than my old lies.

231
00:13:06,860 --> 00:13:07,690
Good.

232
00:13:07,773 --> 00:13:08,952
I'll look forward to it.

233
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:11,020
You guys take care!

234
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:13,065
I hope we meet again sometime!

235
00:13:13,700 --> 00:13:14,530
How come?

236
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:16,477
Well, because I...

237
00:13:16,560 --> 00:13:18,580
Are you antisocial or something?

238
00:13:18,860 --> 00:13:20,937
I'm taking off for life on the high seas,

239
00:13:21,020 --> 00:13:23,497
and I hope that we'll eventually
meet again, that's all!

240
00:13:23,580 --> 00:13:24,857
What are you talking about?

241
00:13:24,940 --> 00:13:27,040
Get on already. Huh?

242
00:13:27,340 --> 00:13:29,540
We're friends, right? So get on.

243
00:13:32,740 --> 00:13:33,960
This is it!

244
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:37,700
I'm really a pirate captain now!

245
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:39,777
Don't be stupid, Usopp!

246
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:40,840
I'm the captain!

247
00:14:02,640 --> 00:14:03,993
There goes the captain.

248
00:14:04,380 --> 00:14:07,877
He fell in with some pretty awesome
people, so I'm not too worried.

249
00:14:07,960 --> 00:14:09,657
Yeah, he'll be safe with them.

250
00:14:09,740 --> 00:14:12,446
I've never seen anybody
as strong as they are.

251
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:14,957
He's always talked
about becoming a pirate,

252
00:14:15,040 --> 00:14:16,777
and now he's headed
off to live his dreams.

253
00:14:16,860 --> 00:14:19,977
You know, the villagers are going to
be sad when we break the news to them.

254
00:14:20,060 --> 00:14:23,417
Our captain was the only person who
could liven things up around here.

255
00:14:23,500 --> 00:14:25,420
Now he's gone.

256
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:29,857
Hey, I just had a great idea!

257
00:14:29,940 --> 00:14:31,260
What is it?

258
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:34,560
Mary? Yes?

259
00:14:35,380 --> 00:14:39,380
Lying hurts, a lot Are you
referring to Klahadore?

260
00:14:41,300 --> 00:14:42,130
No

261
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:45,380
You must be talking about Usopp?

262
00:14:45,940 --> 00:14:48,420
You really wanted him to stay, didn't you?

263
00:14:51,340 --> 00:14:52,520
Miss Kaya

264
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:54,310
Years ago,

265
00:14:54,480 --> 00:14:59,068
one of the villagers told me a story
about your good friend Usopp's childhood.

266
00:15:00,100 --> 00:15:03,997
Only a short time after his father
left the village to become a pirate,

267
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:07,080
his mother, whom he was
very close to, passed away.

268
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:11,910
Pirates!

269
00:15:11,993 --> 00:15:12,880
Pirates are here!

270
00:15:14,960 --> 00:15:16,020
Pirates are here!

271
00:15:16,740 --> 00:15:17,797
Pirates are here, Mom!

272
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:18,710
They're here!

273
00:15:18,793 --> 00:15:19,623
Hold on, Usopp.

274
00:15:19,706 --> 00:15:20,536
You mustn't shout.

275
00:15:20,619 --> 00:15:21,449
Calm down.

276
00:15:22,100 --> 00:15:23,220
Mom, we're saved!

277
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:25,106
Dad finally came back for us!

278
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:28,880
There you go with your
wild imagination again.

279
00:15:29,420 --> 00:15:31,840
You silly boy. It's true!

280
00:15:32,120 --> 00:15:35,477
He always said he'd come back for us and
take us with him when you got better,

281
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:36,442
didn't he, Mom?

282
00:15:37,380 --> 00:15:40,600
Usopp, my dear, your father
won't be coming back.

283
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:47,200
But I'm proud to have married such a
brave man who dared to chase his dreams.

284
00:15:48,540 --> 00:15:50,397
I heard about a special medicine.

285
00:15:50,480 --> 00:15:52,421
This stuff can cure any sickness!

286
00:15:52,920 --> 00:15:53,900
So silly.

287
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:56,400
You dream too much.

288
00:15:56,940 --> 00:15:58,520
I am a dreamer!

289
00:15:58,700 --> 00:15:59,840
And I'm silly!

290
00:16:00,280 --> 00:16:01,120
It's true!

291
00:16:01,280 --> 00:16:02,137
I'm proud of it!

292
00:16:02,220 --> 00:16:04,279
After all, I'm the son of a pirate!

293
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:06,980
Promise me one thing.

294
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:10,300
Promise me you'll grow
up to be brave like him.

295
00:16:17,680 --> 00:16:19,200
PIRATES ARE COMING!

296
00:16:22,100 --> 00:16:23,629
Perhaps out of loneliness,

297
00:16:23,900 --> 00:16:26,957
he continued to shout it
after his mother passed away,

298
00:16:27,040 --> 00:16:31,297
in the hopes that one day his father's
pirate ship would be at the shore?

299
00:16:31,380 --> 00:16:36,300
ready to spirit him away to the sea and
give him a family that he never had.

300
00:16:39,880 --> 00:16:45,200
The villagers say that his outlandish
lies contain his most heartfelt wish.

301
00:16:47,180 --> 00:16:48,010
Pirates!

302
00:16:48,093 --> 00:16:48,937
Pirates are coming!

303
00:16:49,020 --> 00:16:51,860
As someone else who lost both parents,

304
00:16:52,140 --> 00:16:56,905
he saw you as a kindred spirit, and he
couldn't sit by and ignore your suffering.

305
00:16:58,640 --> 00:17:00,500
Now it's time for you, too,

306
00:17:00,660 --> 00:17:03,697
to rise from the ashes
of tragedy and live up

307
00:17:03,780 --> 00:17:06,604
to the example that Usopp
worked so hard to set.

308
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:09,830
Yes.

309
00:17:14,160 --> 00:17:17,520
Cheers to a new ship
and a new Gourmet! Yeah!

310
00:17:21,760 --> 00:17:25,640
They said they were fighting
to live, not to die.

311
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:31,380
Usopp's wild stories and outlandish lies
always spoke of the joy of being alive.

312
00:17:31,900 --> 00:17:36,077
They helped me through my grief by
cheering me up and telling me to live.

313
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:36,990
Indeed.

314
00:17:38,860 --> 00:17:40,820
Okay, we're really doing this?

315
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:42,280
You bet!

316
00:17:42,560 --> 00:17:44,717
We're going to follow in our
great captain's footsteps.

317
00:17:44,800 --> 00:17:46,035
We're going to dance.

318
00:17:48,040 --> 00:17:48,870
Pottery!

319
00:17:49,640 --> 00:17:50,640
Pottery! Pottery!

320
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:51,990
Pottery!

321
00:17:52,073 --> 00:17:52,903
Pottery!

322
00:17:53,620 --> 00:17:54,450
Pottery!

323
00:17:54,533 --> 00:17:56,300
My life starts now, Mary.

324
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:58,720
I'm going to be a doctor.

325
00:17:59,160 --> 00:18:01,020
That's wonderful, Miss Kaya.

326
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:02,682
Just wonderful.

327
00:18:03,940 --> 00:18:04,770
Yay!

328
00:18:04,853 --> 00:18:05,683
Yay, everybody!

329
00:18:07,120 --> 00:18:10,437
As a kid, I never stopped.

330
00:18:10,520 --> 00:18:13,037
Searching for a great treasure!

331
00:18:13,120 --> 00:18:17,777
I had a map in my mind.

332
00:18:17,860 --> 00:18:20,477
That I knew would lead me.

333
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:24,617
I had to find my way to that place!

334
00:18:24,700 --> 00:18:27,497
Before someone could beat me.

335
00:18:27,580 --> 00:18:31,677
The promised land was in my grasp.

336
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:34,380
And I wouldn't let go!

337
00:18:35,860 --> 00:18:38,177
La, la, la, la.

338
00:18:38,260 --> 00:18:39,457
My only dream.

339
00:18:39,540 --> 00:18:41,937
La, la, la, la, la.

340
00:18:42,020 --> 00:18:47,520
I won't stop chasing
it until it comes true!

341
00:18:49,360 --> 00:18:52,917
But if the world ever changes,

342
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:56,397
I call out your name.

343
00:18:56,480 --> 00:19:02,700
We return to the time when
everything's the same.

344
00:19:03,380 --> 00:19:09,537
As long as I'm with you,
my memories don't fade.

345
00:19:09,620 --> 00:19:15,060
Waiting for that one true dream?
